{"agent_id":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T00:42:37.884748794Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"55c73bbe-48d1-4e77-810f-0247f3ad4bda","comment_uuid":"179b486c-3d5e-4d25-96be-c91737d97fdd","author":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","content":"## REVIEW (1/3): Verdict + Wave ordering — CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nIndependent adversarial review of the PLAN comment (2026-08-01 00:34). I read all 10 sub-issues #109-#118, verified claims against the live repo and CLI, and reproduced the #109 defect in this very session. The plan is directionally sound and honestly sequenced, but it has 3 blocking gaps and several hidden dependencies.\n\n### Q1: Is the wave ordering correct?\n\nVERDICT: Mostly correct (0→1→2→3 matches the critical path), but with hidden dependencies and one security-relevant omission.\n\n1. MUST FIX — #113 (bulk-close) has a hidden dependency on #112 (locks). 8 of the stale test issues (#33, #34, #35, #64, #66, #71, #92, #93) are currently locked by OL2r (crosslink locks list). If close refuses on locked issues, #113 stalls. Sequence #112 before #113, or verify close-on-locked behavior first.\n\n2. MUST FIX — #113's selection needs explicit exclusions. Do NOT bulk-close #73/#74 (they are completed but their findings/ deliverables are unmerged — #114 must merge them first, else the tracker loses the only copies of that work), and exclude #106-#108 (the active test cycle) plus #109-#118 (this plan) and #14-#21/#22-#27 (real work). close-all has no status filter in its help; verify it only touches open issues and pass a precise filter.\n\n3. MUST FIX — #109 has an unresolved fork (align enforcement vs deny bash) that determines what Wave 2's docs must say. #114/#115/#116/#117 all touch KICKOFF.md and/or agent templates; #116 and #109 both touch .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts. Decide the #109 direction BEFORE Wave 2 or Wave 2 will need rework. If #109 picks deny-bash, KICKOFF.md's 'Always allowed' section and 'Reviewing Previous Phase Output' (git fetch/diff/show) must be rewritten — a much bigger doc change than #116 currently scopes.\n\n4. SHOULD CONSIDER — Wave ordering is not encoded in the tracker: #109-#118 ALL appear in 'crosslink issue ready' today. Add blocked_by edges so #118 cannot be launched before #109/#111/#117; otherwise a future agent following 'ready' can start Wave 3 early (the exact premature-PASS risk the plan exists to prevent).\n\n5. SHOULD CONSIDER — #112 enabling auto_steal_stale_locks=true is risky as scoped. My own lock on #78 (claimed minutes ago) already displays [STALE] in 'crosslink locks list', and heartbeat hooks are not deployed (workflow diff: all 6 .claude/hooks/*.py missing), so staleness detection cannot distinguish an active agent from an abandoned one. Auto-steal could steal an active agent's lock mid-run — including during Wave 3. Verify the staleness heuristic against active sessions before enabling auto_steal.\n\n6. NIT — Priorities: #109/#110/#111/#112/#118 say 'High.' in their descriptions but are all priority=medium. If the tracker is the triage source (the premise of #113), priorities should match reality.","created_at":"2026-08-01T00:42:37.878927026Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABABt5cDNY6LF3n7LbbBQtsnsNO0IfoENLN0cWS3jRa4/BNIwd1b804/5M0NoQsKVsak9e1lAedc8tYPgvasOs+Dg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGexRGCfVBwxPm4EPi8Ci3To76sfVRiUPTJdU0UUhviB+iMH1qwuPtSw/kvbT1Bopd/dhwehGbmVr62WRaEvdAA="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T00:42:51.402649375Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"55c73bbe-48d1-4e77-810f-0247f3ad4bda","comment_uuid":"43c2233a-c1de-42df-b854-778006393b25","author":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","content":"## REVIEW (2/3): Root cause assessment — #109 CONFIRMED, but the investigation plan is incomplete\n\n### Q2: Is #109 correctly identified as the root cause? Is the approach sound?\n\nVERDICT: The defect is REAL and I reproduced it live in this session. But the denial-origin trace as scoped is missing a critical branch, and fixing #109 in isolation would open a security hole.\n\nLIVE REPRODUCTION: This session runs under .opencode/agents/reviewer.md (frontmatter l.7-14: bash map declaring crosslink/git/ls/cat/cargo/npm allow). The effective permission rules shown to me declare 'git *' and 'ls *' and 'cat *' as ALLOWED — yet every git/ls/cat call is denied; only 'crosslink *' executes. KICKOFF.md's 'Always allowed: git status, git diff...' list is false in practice. This matches #109 exactly.\n\nDENIAL-ORIGIN MAP (new evidence — the plan must account for all four layers):\n1. .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts is NOT LOADED. Neither the repo .opencode/opencode.json nor the global ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json reference it (global plugin array = ./plugins/plugin.ts + ./plugins/interrupt.ts; the global plugin.ts only configures providers). So the plugin's blocked-git and allowed-bash logic is dead code in the current environment.\n2. .claude/hooks/*.py are NOT deployed (crosslink workflow diff lists all 6 missing). .claude/settings.json invokes them with 'if [ -f HOOK ]; then ... else exit 0' — silent fail-open. So NO git-mutation enforcement, NO heartbeat.\n3. The actual denials come from opencode's built-in permission matcher over the frontmatter-derived rules — and the matcher contradicts its own displayed rules (allows listed, deny applied). This is either an opencode matcher bug/version issue (possibly OUTSIDE repo control) or a frontmatter syntax problem (the 'deny' + specific-allow map form may not be interpreted the way it reads).\n4. crosslink kickoff also constructs --allowedTools at launch (config kickoff.allowed_tools is unset); the launcher's construction may override frontmatter. This is the 'build_allowed_tools' lead in #109 — keep it, but it is not the only suspect.\n\nMUST FIX — Security-relevant sequencing hole: today the ONLY thing blocking git push/merge/reset/clean for read-only agents is the blanket bash deny. The frontmatter declares 'git *' allow, which INCLUDES git push. If #109 simply makes the permission layer honor 'git *', read-only agents become git-write-capable with no enforcement layer left (plugin unloaded, hooks missing). #109 must pair the permission fix with deploying an enforcement layer (load crosslink-guard.ts and/or deploy the hooks) — or choose deny-bash-and-rewrite-docs. The plan must add this, and the verification criterion must include 'git push remains blocked for reviewer/auditor'.\n\nSOUNDNESS of the proposed investigation: the trace direction is right, but drop the crosslink-guard.ts hypothesis early (it is not loaded — unless the plan intends to load it, which is itself a scope decision). First cheap discriminator: test whether the deny persists with a minimal frontmatter (bash: allow like builder.md, which reportedly worked in prior AC-1 runs) vs the map form — if the map form is the trigger, the fix is config syntax, not the matcher.\n\nALSO NOTE: #109's claim that hook-config declares cat/grep/find allowed is inaccurate — hook-config.json allowed_bash_prefixes omits cat/grep/find (they exist only in the plugin's DEFAULT_ALLOWED_BASH, which hook-config REPLACES). The 'declared allowed' sources are mutually inconsistent: hook-config allows ls/dir/pwd/echo/git-status..., frontmatter allows git/ls/cat/cargo/npm..., KICKOFF.md promises git read-only. Reconciling all three is part of the fix.","created_at":"2026-08-01T00:42:51.397008664Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAByWNtLpfKHs6/0OR5LKqPHZiTj/FNaFYgCtff3H6fWwbnzAExQ22JMyEBdYkcTEE7zrQRMebFOgFDrtGNqS0BA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMOHs+W/PUTZy9ukW5nscUC9Xp+xQ2zk/nVBQ111QEQrECyqkui2C8rC2svCo/aPLY97w2wsmfAbCAzLdcIAkgQ="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T00:43:07.001048753Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"55c73bbe-48d1-4e77-810f-0247f3ad4bda","comment_uuid":"c025f8ca-9830-468f-b30c-65cc06cba594","author":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","content":"## REVIEW (3/3): Gaps + Wave 3 design — the final gate is right in principle, under-specified in practice\n\n### Q3: Gaps — missing fixes, risks, steps that belong in the plan\n\n1. MUST FIX — Artifact handoff mechanism is UNDEFINED (the biggest Wave 3 gap). KICKOFF.md states 'Cross-worktree filesystem access is blocked'. AC-1's test-output.txt lives in the builder worktree; reviewer/auditor worktrees cannot reach it. The re-run must specify the mechanism: (a) shared /tmp path (builder frontmatter allows /tmp; prior cycles used /tmp artifacts successfully), or (b) git-based handoff (commit artifact + git fetch . branch + git show) — but note git fetch is NOT in any allowed list today, so option (b) requires the #109 fix to cover it. Then the re-run must prove DOWNSTREAM CONSUMPTION: the reviewer must assert on the artifact content, not a self-contained check (the exact sidestep #118's audit flagged).\n\n2. MUST FIX — Wave 3 PASS criteria are undefined. Closing #78 needs explicit criteria: original AC-1..AC-4 PLUS (i) artifact handoff demonstrated with downstream consumption; (ii) dependency edges present (#111) AND launch-time behavior verified — I found NO evidence that kickoff/swarm enforces blocked_by at launch (the crosslink-guide skill documents 'ready' as advisory; #106-#108 all currently list as ready). If enforcement is process-only, the plan must say so and verify the edges instead of claiming machine enforcement; (iii) all 3 phases post plan+result comments per #117; (iv) auditor completes.\n\n3. MUST FIX — Model selection + timeout for Wave 3 unspecified. North Mini free looped 31 min without completing; big-pickle completed the audit in ~8 min. Pin models for the re-run (e.g., ling/nemotron for builder/reviewer, big-pickle for auditor) or define an explicit max-runtime and failure criterion, else the gate can stall on model lottery.\n\n4. SHOULD CONSIDER — Use FRESH phase issues for the re-run, not #106-#108: they carry prior comments/history, and reusing them invites the duplicate-plan confusion #115 is meant to fix. New issues should bake in the artifact path, dependency edges, and parent #78 link at creation.\n\n5. SHOULD CONSIDER — 'Hooks not deployed' (audit finding #6) has no home in the plan. It contributes to stale-lock misdetection (no heartbeat) and zero git-mutation enforcement. Fold it into #112 or #109.\n\n6. SHOULD CONSIDER — #116 scope misses the invalid 'crosslink comment' form: KICKOFF.md step 4 ('crosslink comment 78 ...' — confirmed: unrecognized subcommand), .crosslink/rules/global.md l.130/l.196, .crosslink/rules/tracking-normal.md l.60. Fix along with the 'crosslink intervene' references.\n\n7. SHOULD CONSIDER — Findings persistence (#114) interacts with Wave 3: if the auditor posts observations but findings docs still don't exist, the documented two-stage consolidation cannot run. Either include a consolidation step in Wave 3 or explicitly scope it out. And #73/#74 must be merged (or their docs cherry-picked) BEFORE #113 closes them.\n\n8. NIT — #118's description names only #109+#111 as preconditions; it should also require the Wave 2 template fixes (#115/#116/#117), since the re-run agents will follow KICKOFF.md.\n\n### Q4: Is Wave 3 (artifact handoff + dependency enforcement) the right final gate?\n\nVERDICT: Right gate, wrong execution unit. Keeping #78 open until a real 3-phase run completes is correct and directly addresses the premature-PASS lesson. But as scoped, #118 inherits the exact failure mode it was created to prevent: without a defined handoff mechanism, defined PASS criteria, pinned models, and a decision on whether 'dependency enforcement' is machine or process, the re-run can again validate three independent agents and be declared PASS. The gate is only honest once items 1-3 above are specified in the plan.\n\n### NOTABLE POSITIVES\n- The plan correctly puts the sandbox defect first — it poisoned diagnosis (3 AC-3 failures misattributed to models) and blocks every read-only phase.\n- Sub-issue decomposition maps 1:1 to the audit's recommendations; every file:line target in #114/#116 that I checked is accurate.\n- #113's --no-changelog discipline and #112's lock cleanup are the right housekeeping, and the wave ordering 0→1→2→3 is sound on the critical path.\n- The plan honestly surfaces its own open decision (align vs deny bash) rather than hiding it.\n\nBottom line: approve the direction; rework #109 to include enforcement deployment + the align/deny decision point, add the handoff mechanism + PASS criteria + model pinning to #118, and re-sequence #113 after #112 with explicit exclusions. Then the re-run is a credible gate.","created_at":"2026-08-01T00:43:06.994956603Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAB80IPQDjXN3nbkb8mGe299DctTGnAy2Mu8KEf9QSnjlgivk7MrqUYrReMcq5NEGDkFQnlTeTAlprezcj09gyBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDnU6xNatB7y7ej1/Xzg/fbTGhUEmZOErS/Oh3DS/cGenoJWpqh1CLXB89i8Hpfi1o7mq3jDBhNboT70FsRnjw8="}
